  <reporting-org ref="XI-IATI-IADB" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inter-American Development Bank</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Apoyo a la Implementacin de la Poltica Nacional de Seguridad Vial</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support National Road Safety Policy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Road safety has been declared a State policy in Colombia. The
present governments National Development Plan includes road safety as
one of its principal strategies, and the Congress of the Republic has established it as
a priority in its work program. In this context, development of an institutional
framework for road safety management is one of the priority actions of the National
Road Safety Plan.

The purpose of this operation is to
consolidate the institutional strengthening process and further contribute to the
execution of the priority actions on Colombias road safety management agenda.

The main objective of the program is to support the Colombian
government in the consolidation of the national road safety policy, the ultimate goal
of which will be to reduce the number of fatalities and injuries caused by traffic
accidents, through: (i) institutional strengthening for the implementation and
dissemination of the PNSV; (ii) consolidation of the National Road Safety
Observatory; and (iii) support for the formulation of local and regional road safety
plans.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES"></narrative>
  </description>
